Not included
------------

@xzdarcy/react-timeline-editor is MIT but depends on React. This app is
vanilla JavaScript, so the library was not added.

@ffmpeg/ffmpeg is MIT. Desktop and web export already use the native ffmpeg
binary, so the wasm build was not added.

OpenCut (https://github.com/OpenCut-app/OpenCut) is MIT. It is a separate
application and was not vendored. Its track, playhead, trim, and snap layout
was used as a design reference only.

Shotcut, Kdenlive, and Olive are GPL. No code was copied from them.
CapCut and Vegas are proprietary. Their timeline layout (playhead, trim,
ripple, snapping, J/K/L shuttle) was used as a design reference only.
